WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.159 --> 00:00:02.738
Hi, welcome back to Lam Rim.

00:00:02.738 --> 00:00:05.465
Remember we're going
through these seven steps

00:00:05.465 --> 00:00:10.460
to reach that place where
we have this feeling

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.280
of jumping between planets,

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.140
and helping people on
all of those planets.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:18.690
This kind of vision of a bodhisattva.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.400
We're on the third of them.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.160
So MAR SHES means you recognize

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.087
that all the people around
you have been your mom.

00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:29.930
And then DRIN DRAN we finished,

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.050
which was remember all the cool things

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.700
they did to take care of you.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.630
Basically, that you didn't die

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:40.750
and you got to be an adult
because of their hard work

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.670
every single minute of the day,

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:46.430
and also really suffering
from the financial burden

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.110
of bringing you up.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.480
Now we reach the third great category

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.583
which is called DRIN GZO.

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:55.770
DRIN is short for BKA' DRIN

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.470
which means kindness.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:00.278
GZO BA means to fix it,

00:01:00.278 --> 00:01:01.928
which means to pay it back.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:05.760
So DRIN GZO means if my moms

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.650
have been that nice to me,

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.700
then what can I do to pay them back?

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.810
How can I pay them back?

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.277
I like this.

00:01:14.277 --> 00:01:16.743
I think it's very appropriate here

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:21.640
if we add a special verse from
the Three Principal Paths.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.650
I've inserted this verse

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:29.410
because I think it's
especially relevant here.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:31.140
It goes like this.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.650
I just remember this verse a lot.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.203
I think about it a lot.

00:01:36.203 --> 00:01:38.460
,SHUGS DRAG CHU BO BZHI
YI RGYUN GYIS KHYER,

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.943
,ZLOG DKA' LAS KYI
'CHING BA DAM POS BSDAMS,

00:01:40.943 --> 00:01:44.468
,BDAG 'DZIN LCAGS KYI
DRA BA'I SPUBS SU TSUD,

00:01:44.468 --> 00:01:47.000
,MA RIG MUN PA'I SMAG CHEN KUN NAS 'THIBS,

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.319
,MU MED SRID PAR SKYE ZHING SKYE BA RU,

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:51.823
,SDUG BSNGAL GSUM GYIS
RGYUN CHAD MED PAR MNAR,

00:01:51.823 --> 00:01:54.527
,GNAS SKABS 'DI 'DRAR
GYUR PA'I MA RNAMS KYI,

00:01:54.527 --> 00:01:57.950
,NGANG TSUL BSAMS NAS SEMS
MCHOG BSKYED BAR MDZOD,

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.180
This is in the Three Principal Paths,

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.530
Je Tsongkapa's way of
introducing this idea

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.100
of paying back your mom's kindness.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.063
I was in Mongolia many years ago.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.550
I guess it was the 90's.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.173
They had just got their independence.

00:02:21.378 --> 00:02:23.700
So religion was allowed again

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.700
for the first time in about 75 years.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:32.350
It was an exciting time to be in Mongolia.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:36.170
So I said I would give a talk

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.890
along with a great teacher,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.828
a great lama, named Bakula Rinpoche.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.130
It was at a stadium.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.747
It was at the largest,

00:02:47.747 --> 00:02:49.660
the place they could do it in Mongolia,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.930
which is actually where they
hold the national circus

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:55.200
which is the biggest stadium in Mongolia.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.400
We had a lot of people.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.340
I remember I used this verse.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.648
I started out with this verse

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:05.200
and I was looking at a family.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.980
I was talking about how they would feel

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.260
if their daughter turned
out to be their mom.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.120
What if your daughter

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.437
turned out to have been your mom before?

00:03:18.437 --> 00:03:21.480
And I read this verse and
I explained this verse.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.283
I remember.

00:03:23.283 --> 00:03:26.682
Afterwards there was a family
came up to me and they said,

00:03:26.682 --> 00:03:28.850
"Please take it back."

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.340
I said, "What?"

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.600
And they said, "Take it back.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.017
"Don't talk about our
daughter with this verse.

00:03:36.017 --> 00:03:38.320
"It's too dark.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.570
"We don't want to use this
verse about our daughter."

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.040
So it was a very,

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.090
I think they were very sensitive

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.500
to the real meaning of the verse.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.240
The verse is very dark and very sad.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:57.240
It's necessary when we think
about paying our mom back

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.880
for the kindness she gave to us.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.830
We have to think of our mom in this way.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.650
So let go through the Tibetan

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:07.160
of Tsongkapa's

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.549
Three Principal Paths.

00:04:08.549 --> 00:04:11.053
SHUGS DRAG CHU BO BZHI YI RGYUN GYIS KHYER

00:04:11.053 --> 00:04:15.357
They are swept away by
four fierce river currents,

00:04:16.523 --> 00:04:18.570
ZLOG DKA' LAS KYI 'CHING BA DAM POS BSDAMS

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.410
chained up tight in past
deeds, hard to undo.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:26.600
They are swept away by, for example,

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.584
the suffering of being born,

00:04:29.584 --> 00:04:31.110
SKYE RGA NA 'CHI

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:34.490
of getting old, of
getting sick and of dying.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:37.352
There are our mom.

00:04:37.352 --> 00:04:41.970
Our mom has fallen into this great river.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.727
This very fast river

00:04:43.727 --> 00:04:46.530
and she's been swept downstream.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:50.080
The river is SKYE RGA NA 'CHI.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:54.450
She has the suffering
of going through birth

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:57.500
and then she has the suffering of aging.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.690
Every moment since the moment she's born,

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:05.690
an unstoppable aging, like
a candle burning down.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:09.470
Then she's often times sick in this life.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:14.470
I translated for the Dalai
Lama's doctor for some years,

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:19.760
two of the greatest Tibetans
doctors in the world.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:23.923
And I was kind of shocked one day he said,

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.307
He was given a talk, he said,

00:05:27.307 --> 00:05:32.307
"By the way health is not
normal. Health is abnormal.

00:05:32.737 --> 00:05:34.050
"Disease is normal."

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.330
And I said, "What?"

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.957
And he said, "It's normal for
your elements of your body

00:05:39.957 --> 00:05:41.470
"to be out of balance."

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:44.527
That's normal state of human being.

00:05:44.527 --> 00:05:49.527
Then to be healthy is
like very rare balance

00:05:49.547 --> 00:05:51.330
of all the elements in your body.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.750
The human condition, the normal
condition of human being,

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.290
is to be sick.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.810
And if you're health for awhile,

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.410
that's just really dumb good luck

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:05.030
that you're healthy for awhile.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.155
So SKYE RGA NA 'CHI

00:06:07.155 --> 00:06:08.550
and then our mom must die.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:13.550
So our moms, those beautiful
people who have been our mom,

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:17.200
they are being swept downstream

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.253
by these four kinds of suffering.

00:06:19.253 --> 00:06:20.878
,SHUGS DRAG CHU BO BZHI
YI RGYUN GYIS KHYER,

00:06:20.878 --> 00:06:23.478
,BZLOG DKA' LAS KYI
'CHING BA DAM POS BSDAMS,

00:06:23.478 --> 00:06:25.520
And that's okay

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:30.320
if you're being swept
downstream on a river.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:31.900
Well you could try to swim

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.910
And you could try to swim to the shore.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.770
But their hands are chained

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:37.823
and their legs are chained.

00:06:37.823 --> 00:06:41.113
Their hands and legs are chained together.

00:06:41.113 --> 00:06:43.479
ZLOG DKA' LAS KYI 'CHING BA

00:06:43.479 --> 00:06:45.450
The karma chains.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:49.200
Maybe if they weren't
chained they could swim

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.220
and maybe they could
try to get to the shore.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.436
But they are chained.

00:06:53.436 --> 00:06:55.794
Their hands are chained.
Their feet are chained

00:06:55.794 --> 00:06:57.870
by the past karma.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:02.120
They don't really have a
choice. They don't have options.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.260
They don't have option
to change the direction

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.830
of their life.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.250
The direction of their life

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:09.900
is largely determined

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.660
by what they did in their past lives.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:15.182
So they don't have options

00:07:15.182 --> 00:07:18.640
to try to do something
like save themselves.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:19.873
They are chained up.

00:07:19.873 --> 00:07:21.310
Throw your...

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.550
Take your mom, throw her off a cliff

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:26.191
into a raging river,

00:07:26.191 --> 00:07:28.650
but before your throw her off the cliff,

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.172
chain her arms and legs together.

00:07:31.172 --> 00:07:33.137
Think of it that way.

00:07:33.137 --> 00:07:35.870
BDAG 'DZIN LCAGS KYI
DRA BA'I SBUBS SU TSUD

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:38.740
Then, just before your
throw her off the cliff,

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.790
a lock her in an iron box.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:44.110
Like an iron cage.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:47.860
So first of all, chain her hands and legs.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.913
And just for good measure

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.110
put her into like a... Zoo cage?

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:57.470
A cage for the animals at the zoo.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.570
Put her into a cage like that.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.290
And then throw that into the river.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:05.660
Cause that's the chance she's
going to have to escape.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.060
Which is zero.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:12.060
Then, what's the cage? It's BDAG 'DZIN

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.450
It's a misunderstanding her world.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:19.480
For example, misunderstanding

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:23.403
why your husband's yelling
at you, in that moment.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.050
When you don't understand...

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:27.550
When you come into the kitchen

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.740
and your husband starts yelling at you

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:32.890
and you don't understand what's going on

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.500
and you yell back.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:37.730
In a way, you are in a iron cage.

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:40.430
You have just put
yourself in an iron cage.

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:44.610
So now think about this mom

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:45.890
who brought you up,

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:48.940
who kept you from being like an animal.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:53.810
And now, she's thrown
into this terrible river.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.290
Powerful river.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:58.800
And her hands are chained
and her legs are chained

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.480
by the karma she did in the past.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.860
And, on top of that, the chained mom

00:09:06.204 --> 00:09:09.501
is shoved into a cage. A small cage.

00:09:09.501 --> 00:09:12.821
And then that is thrown into the river.

00:09:12.821 --> 00:09:15.720
MU MED SRID PAR SKYE ZHING SKYE BA RU

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.393
They are born... You
guys know MU GSUM MU BZHI

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.883
Three... What do you
call it? Parameter, no.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:27.560
Permutation, three or four permutations.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:31.750
This MU MED means countless permutations.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.643
It's a interested word.

00:09:33.643 --> 00:09:37.236
MU MED means countless permutations.

00:09:37.236 --> 00:09:38.730
SKYE ZHING SKYE BA RU

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:41.660
She's born in countless forms.

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:44.290
Animals, different kinds of birds,

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:48.008
different kinds of fish,
different kinds of humans.

00:09:48.008 --> 00:09:50.970
SDUG BSNGAL GSUM GYIS
RGYUN CHAD MED PAR MNAR

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:54.698
And she is suffering from
the three kinds of suffering.

00:09:54.698 --> 00:09:56.420
RGYUN CHAD MED PA

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:00.280
He is returning to the image
of a stream of a river.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:03.310
And without a break in that flow,

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:06.043
she is suffering from those
three kinds of suffering.

00:10:06.043 --> 00:10:07.353
SDUG BSNGAL GYI SDUG BSNGAL

00:10:07.353 --> 00:10:08.494
'GYUR BA'I SDUG BSNGAL

00:10:08.494 --> 00:10:10.177
and KHYAB PA 'DU BYED KYI SDUG BSNGAL

00:10:10.177 --> 00:10:12.299
What's SDUG BSNGAL GYI SDUG BSNGAL?

00:10:12.299 --> 00:10:13.674
Suffering of suffering.

00:10:13.674 --> 00:10:16.579
What's the classical example?

00:10:16.579 --> 00:10:18.313
A backache, or a foot ache.

00:10:20.177 --> 00:10:21.470
SDUG BSNGAL GYI SDUG BSNGAL

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:25.208
Then second one 'GYUR BA'I SDUG BSNGAL

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:29.680
Every time you get a nice dinner,

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.950
it changes, you get hungry again.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.400
So suffering of change.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.716
And then KHYAB PA 'DU BYED KYI SDUG BSNGAL

00:10:35.716 --> 00:10:38.207
KHYAB PA means covers everywhere.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.840
That basically aging.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:46.810
That we live in a body which is mortal.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.497
So that's,

00:10:48.497 --> 00:10:49.977
KHYAB PA 'DU BYED KYI SDUG BSNGAL

00:10:49.977 --> 00:10:52.760
also covers the first two.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:57.760
So it's just our nature to fall apart.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.240
As you get older, you will have the joy

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.990
of having your body fall apart.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:05.248
Then you exercise, exercise,

00:11:05.248 --> 00:11:06.673
and then it keeps falling apart.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:12.043
It's like holding up a
sand castle or something.

00:11:12.043 --> 00:11:14.159
GNAS SKABS 'DI 'DRAR
GYUR PA'I MA RNAMS KYI

00:11:14.159 --> 00:11:17.160
NGANG TSUL BSAMS NAS SEMS
MCHOG BSKYED PAR MDZOD

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:20.370
Think about, try to imagine

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:24.860
that all the people around
you have been your mom.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:28.060
Try to imagine that they have been thrown

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:32.020
into a terrible river
with their hands chained,

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:35.390
stuffed into an iron cage.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:39.290
And in that cage, underwater, struggling,

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:43.190
they are going through direct pain.

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:44.690
They are going through seeing

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:47.910
every nice thing collapse in their life.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:51.390
While they're going through that

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:55.822
their body is also falling apart.

00:11:55.822 --> 00:11:59.340
Let's imagine your mom.

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:02.800
Even your mom just in
this life is like that.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.550
Her situation is super desperate.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:10.070
To jump off the banks of the river,

00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:13.370
to swim down underwater,
to open up their iron cage,

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:15.230
to get the chains off of her,

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:18.637
to pull her out of the
water, to get her to safety,

00:12:18.637 --> 00:12:20.630
it's almost impossible.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:25.200
Difficult. But at least
we should try to imagine

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.880
that it's something we would like to do.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:30.910
So that gets you in the mind frame

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:32.130
of the third step

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:33.830
for developing bodhichitta,

00:12:35.026 --> 00:12:36.920
Bodhisattva vision,

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:39.990
which is that you're,

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:42.680
if you want to pay your mom back

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.439
just get her out of the river.

00:12:44.439 --> 00:12:45.470
Get her out of the cage.

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:48.270
Get her out of the handcuffs.

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:52.160
Paying your mom back for
everything she did for you

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:57.070
doesn't mean buy her new TV
when she's too old to work.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:13:01.996
It's a little more complicated than that.

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.500
Let's go on to the next verse,

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.871
first verse of this section actually.

00:13:07.871 --> 00:13:10.080
BSLAB BTUS LAS

00:13:11.224 --> 00:13:16.156
BSLAB BTUS is called Shiksasamuccaya.

00:13:16.156 --> 00:13:16.989
Shantideva,

00:13:16.989 --> 00:13:21.841
Master Shantideva wrote two
great books that we have.

00:13:21.841 --> 00:13:23.157
Of course the first one is

00:13:23.157 --> 00:13:25.470
The Guide To The
Bodhisattva's Way Of Life.

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.350
And the other is a long description

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:31.867
of sutra quotations

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:36.582
that applied to training ourselves.

00:13:36.582 --> 00:13:39.897
That's called Compendium of Trainings.

00:13:39.897 --> 00:13:41.363
NYON MONGS KYIS SMYO

00:13:41.363 --> 00:13:43.540
Your mom.

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.531
Imagine your mom.

00:13:45.531 --> 00:13:48.250
SMYO means gone crazy,

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.841
like she went crazy.

00:13:50.841 --> 00:13:54.205
Like I have a friend her mom,

00:13:54.205 --> 00:13:56.580
this is in fact, this is a
big danger for older people

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.104
that they take their drugs wrong.

00:13:59.104 --> 00:14:01.610
They forget they took their drugs already

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:04.290
and they take them three
or four times in a day,

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:07.740
or they take whole bottle by accident

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.147
and then they get crazy.

00:14:10.147 --> 00:14:13.983
So imagine NYON MONGS KYIS SMYO

00:14:13.983 --> 00:14:18.970
Your mom has gone crazy.

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:22.640
because of her mental afflictions,

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.963
her negative emotions.

00:14:24.963 --> 00:14:29.930
GTI MUG LDONGS means her misunderstanding

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:33.380
of where life is coming
from has made her blind.

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:37.433
Her misunderstanding gouged out her eyes.

00:14:37.433 --> 00:14:39.540
G-YANG SA MANG PO'I LAM DU NI

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:44.193
She's wandering in the high mountains

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:46.930
near all of these cliffs.

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:51.530
So she's blind and she's gone crazy,

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:55.610
and she's balancing on,
high in the Himalayas,

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:59.865
on these very dangerous cliffs.

00:14:59.865 --> 00:15:01.715
GOM PA RE RE RDEG 'CHA' BA

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:07.750
Then you're watching her
take her unsteady steps

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:12.750
near the edge of these
deep abysses, deep chasms.

00:15:13.286 --> 00:15:16.790
BDAG DANG GZHAN RTAG MYA NGAN GZHI

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.220
'GRO BA RNAMS NI SDUG BSNGAL MTSUNGS

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:22.136
So BDAG DANG GZHAN RTAG MYA NGAN GZHI

00:15:22.136 --> 00:15:25.677
Our whole life is a misery.

00:15:25.677 --> 00:15:27.888
'GRO BA RNAMS NI SDUG BSNGAL MTSUNGS

00:15:27.888 --> 00:15:29.870
And the suffering

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:31.770
of living beings is similar

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:36.410
to a person who has gone mad,

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:40.280
and who is blinded, had
their eyes gouged out,

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:44.510
and is walking along these
high mountain canyons

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:47.662
where they could fall off easily.

00:15:47.662 --> 00:15:49.164
ZHES GSUNGS PA LTAR, DPER NA,

00:15:49.164 --> 00:15:51.172
TSE 'DI' AA MA MIG LONG ZHING

00:15:51.172 --> 00:15:53.200
LONG KHRID DANG BRAL

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:57.530
Imagine your mom in this life, MIG LONG,

00:15:57.530 --> 00:16:00.506
her eyes have been cut out.

00:16:00.506 --> 00:16:02.139
LONG KHRID DANG BRAL means

00:16:02.139 --> 00:16:05.100
imagine she has no one to guide her,

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:09.310
Aad she's just, like
thinking of your mom is blind

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:11.010
and she's walking through New York city

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.890
through the traffic.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:16.560
And no one to help her
to get to the other side.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:17.820
SEMS MYOS TE

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:22.150
On top of that she's
gone temporarily insane.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:25.602
On top of being blind, she's insane

00:16:25.602 --> 00:16:29.210
MYOS TE G-YANG SA ZHIG GI
KHAR MCHONG BAR NYE BA NA

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.760
and she's close to falling
off a very high cliff.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:34.933
MCHONG means to jump.

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:39.403
But here it means to fall
off a very high cliff.

00:16:39.403 --> 00:16:42.912
BU DE DER YOD NA

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:48.320
If her daughter or her son is nearby

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.841
at her side,

00:16:50.841 --> 00:16:54.130
AA MA DES KYANG BU DE LA MI RE NA

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:57.420
if she can't hope,

00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:01.202
if she can't put her hopes
in her child at her side,

00:17:01.202 --> 00:17:02.130
then who else

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:04.480
is she going to put her hopes in?

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:07.830
If her child, her daughter or her son,

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:12.020
is walking next to her
through New York City traffic

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:14.620
while the mom is temporarily insane

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:19.130
and also blind, and if
that son or daughter

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:20.860
will not reach their hand out

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:24.070
and help them across the street,

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:25.550
then who can she hope?

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:27.895
Who else is she going to hope for?

00:17:27.895 --> 00:17:31.550
BU DES KYANG AA MA DE MI
BSKYAB NA SU LA BSKYAB

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.350
If the child is going to protect someone

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:36.480
in their whole life,

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.500
if they're going to help someone

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.520
but they don't help their mom

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:43.586
when they are temporarily insane and blind

00:17:43.586 --> 00:17:46.203
and about to die, because they're
going to fall off a cliff,

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:50.897
if the time has come to help her

00:17:50.897 --> 00:17:53.020
and you don't help your own mom,

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:55.290
well then, who else you going to help?

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:58.093
How can you say you're a nice person?

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.730
How can you say you're
doing all this charity work

00:18:03.210 --> 00:18:06.700
if you won't help your own
mom who's right next to you,

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:08.860
and who's going to die
in the next few minutes

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:12.103
if you don't grab her and help her?

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:17.260
Picture here we can see...

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:19.830
I was trying to find a picture somebody

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:22.780
running away from a fire.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.080
It's not very good, right?

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.680
It looks like a thief or something.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:29.305
But, I guess the website
that I used for pictures

00:18:29.305 --> 00:18:30.933
they're all cheerful,

00:18:32.592 --> 00:18:33.810
which is why I use it.

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:37.660
But anyway, imagine that this is your mom.

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:41.550
She's running from a fire in her home.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:44.010
You are standing at the door.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:47.235
You can just step in and take her hand

00:18:47.235 --> 00:18:48.534
and bring her out.

00:18:48.534 --> 00:18:50.050
And you don't.

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:52.310
Just imagine that you don't.

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:55.607
That's the feeling we're
supposed to get here.

00:18:55.607 --> 00:18:57.524
DE BSHIN DU SEMS CAN
THAMS CAD KYAG CHOS DANG

00:18:57.524 --> 00:19:01.057
CHOS MA YIN PA'I BLANG DOR
LTA BA'I MIG DANG NI BRAL

00:19:01.057 --> 00:19:03.740
Every living being around us is blind.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:06.400
People in the whole world
around us are blind,

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:09.320
especially if they don't
have any dharma training.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:13.730
They don't know what's
the right thing to do

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:15.530
and what's the wrong thing to do.

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:20.530
Their judgment of what's
a good thing to do,

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:22.930
of what's a healthy thing to do

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:25.500
and what's a unhealthy thing to do,

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:30.500
their judgment about that
line is completely mistaken.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.910
So even if they think about it

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:34.600
they're going to make the wrong decisions

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.420
about everything.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:39.440
In that sense they are blind.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:43.050
If you had a few minutes

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.400
or a few dollars extra,

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:48.590
if you studied Lam Rim,
then you would use it

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:51.350
to serve somebody else who needed help.

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:52.550
Or you would use the money

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:54.890
to help someone else who needed help.

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:58.760
But if you're blind, then you
would just buy a nice dinner

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.440
or something.

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:02.410
You would ignore those people.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:04.735
That's blindness.

00:20:04.735 --> 00:20:06.660
To not serve the poor,

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:08.940
to not serve people who are sick,

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:11.850
to not serve the environment,

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:14.580
it's a blindness. And
people are just blind.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:17.520
And they're doing the
completely wrong thing.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.160
So imagine your mom like that.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:22.534
SKAD CIG RE RE ZHING 'DOD PA DANG

00:20:22.534 --> 00:20:24.350
LAG LEN PHYIN CI LOG TU BYED PA

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:26.700
All of their hopes in life,

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.540
all of the goals they try to reach,

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.327
are completely mistaken.

00:20:32.327 --> 00:20:35.170
LOG TU BYED PA'I NYES SPYOD
KYIS GOM PA RDEG 'CHA'

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:38.070
So every step they take in their life

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:42.120
is like a person dancing on a high cliff

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.920
and about to fall off.

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:46.620
Every step they take through life

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:49.843
with their eyes blinded is a dangerous,

00:20:49.843 --> 00:20:53.087
is a dangerous step.

00:20:53.087 --> 00:20:54.829
'DI BYED DANG 'DI MA BYED ZER BA'I

00:20:54.829 --> 00:20:57.810
SLOB MKAHN BSHES GNYEN GYI
LONG KHRID DANG NI BRAL

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:02.810
They don't have anyone
who can take their arm

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.450
and guide them across the busy traffic,

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:07.380
or something like that.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:09.707
Here it's called BSHES GNYEN, right?

00:21:09.707 --> 00:21:12.740
DGE BA'I BSHES GNYEN - spiritual friend.

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:16.450
They don't have, most people in this world

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:19.860
don't have anybody who can grab their arm

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:21.020
and say, Come on,

00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:23.440
help other people.

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:25.730
You want to be happy? Help other people.

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:27.580
That's the only way to be happy.

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:31.494
Take care of other people.
They don't have someone.

00:21:31.494 --> 00:21:33.420
'DI BYED DANG 'DI MA BYED ZER

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:36.500
They don't have anybody who can tell them:

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:38.920
do this and don't do this.

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:42.499
This is a good thing to do.
That's a bad thing to do.

00:21:42.499 --> 00:21:46.442
NYON MONGS DUG GSUM GYI
GDON GYIS SEMS DKRUNGS

00:21:46.442 --> 00:21:47.769
NYON MONGS DUG GSUM

00:21:47.769 --> 00:21:52.270
means the three animals at the
middle of the Wheel of Life:

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:57.270
misunderstanding your world,
and then ignorant liking,

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:58.830
and ignorant disliking.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:01.540
Is it okay to like things? Yes.

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:03.883
Is it okay to like things

00:22:03.883 --> 00:22:06.560
and try to take them away
from other people? No.

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:08.880
That's ignorant liking.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:10.390
Is it okay to dislike things?

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:13.690
Yes, we should dislike cancer.

00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:16.270
Is it okay to dislike
cancer in a way that you

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:17.950
take resources from other people?

00:22:17.950 --> 00:22:20.142
I heard today...

00:22:20.142 --> 00:22:23.650
Yes, some country was
blocking vaccinations

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:24.483
to another country

00:22:24.483 --> 00:22:27.462
because they want it
all of them themselves.

00:22:27.462 --> 00:22:31.120
And that's ignorant.

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:32.072
All right.

00:22:32.072 --> 00:22:33.846
DUG GSUM GYI GDON

00:22:33.846 --> 00:22:35.870
GDON means a demon.

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:37.411
GDON GYIS SEMS DKRUGS

00:22:37.411 --> 00:22:40.077
DKRUGS means to...

00:22:40.077 --> 00:22:42.058
Here's DKRUGS

00:22:42.058 --> 00:22:46.103
I got this carrot juice
and if I wanted to...

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:49.380
This is called DKRUGS.

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.690
DKRUGS means to shake it up.

00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:53.623
That's how you make a nice carrot juice

00:22:53.623 --> 00:22:55.156
or something like that.

00:22:55.156 --> 00:22:57.043
Let's see if it tastes good.

00:22:57.043 --> 00:22:58.752
(people chuckle)

00:22:59.910 --> 00:23:01.873
So that's called DKRUGS.

00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:07.100
The people around us are
DKRUGS by the demon of

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:13.453
these three kinds of negative emotions.

00:23:14.592 --> 00:23:18.392
SHES PA LA RANG DBANG MA THOB PAS SMYO

00:23:18.392 --> 00:23:19.700
They cannot...

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:21.023
This is an interesting expression

00:23:21.023 --> 00:23:23.106
SHES PA LA RANG DBANG

00:23:23.106 --> 00:23:26.130
RANG DBANG means freedom or liberation.

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:28.980
Freedom in a political sense, for example.

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:31.587
They don't have RANG DBANG

00:23:31.587 --> 00:23:33.440
about their own mind.

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:38.230
They don't have freedom
to think pure thoughts

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:40.807
because they're out of control.

00:23:40.807 --> 00:23:43.860
SMYO means crazy.

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:47.488
What's the word for alcohol
in ancient scripture?

00:23:49.919 --> 00:23:51.950
We call it SMYO BYED...SMYO BYED.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:55.543
SMYO BYED means crazy
maker, makes you crazy.

00:23:55.543 --> 00:23:56.834
SMYO NAS

00:23:56.834 --> 00:23:59.517
BSKAL PA MANG POR ME DANG LUS DBYER MED DU

00:23:59.517 --> 00:24:01.280
'GYUR BA'I NGAN SONG

00:24:01.280 --> 00:24:03.590
They are about to fall off the cliff

00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:07.950
into the deep canyon called

00:24:07.950 --> 00:24:09.810
the three lower realms.

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:13.876
Where for many BSKAL PAs,
for many millions of years,

00:24:13.876 --> 00:24:15.810
ME DANG LUS DBYER MED

00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:20.560
your body and the fire
there are indistinguishable

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:21.410
one from the other.

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:23.600
You can't tell where your body starts

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:25.881
and where the fire starts.

00:24:25.881 --> 00:24:28.072
NGAN SONG GI G-YANG SA CHEN POR

00:24:28.072 --> 00:24:30.260
They're about to fall off that cliff.

00:24:30.260 --> 00:24:31.826
'GRO BA 'DI LA

00:24:31.826 --> 00:24:35.070
DA LAN RANG CAG DGE BA'I
BSHES GNYEN DANG MJAL

00:24:35.070 --> 00:24:38.903
But us guys, RANG CAG

00:24:38.903 --> 00:24:41.220
DGE BA'I BSHES GNYEN DANG MJAL

00:24:41.220 --> 00:24:43.510
we have met with a spiritual teacher.

00:24:43.510 --> 00:24:45.890
We had the great, good fortune

00:24:45.890 --> 00:24:48.823
to meet awesome spiritual teachers.

00:24:48.823 --> 00:24:51.450
THEG PA CHEN PO'I CHOS DANG PHRAD

00:24:51.450 --> 00:24:56.450
We have made contact
with the Mahayana dharma.

00:24:56.740 --> 00:25:00.290
With the dharma that says,
take care of other people.

00:25:00.290 --> 00:25:03.260
Just to meet somebody who tells you

00:25:03.260 --> 00:25:07.250
to take care of other
people is extremely rare.

00:25:07.250 --> 00:25:10.870
To me, when you talk about
religions of the world:

00:25:10.870 --> 00:25:13.170
Christianity, Islam,

00:25:13.170 --> 00:25:16.393
Hinduism, Judaism,

00:25:17.430 --> 00:25:20.690
they are all very rare, good luck.

00:25:20.690 --> 00:25:24.200
Like don't focus on the
difference between them.

00:25:24.200 --> 00:25:27.870
To meet any of them as a child,

00:25:27.870 --> 00:25:32.040
or to grow up in a country
where any of them exist,

00:25:32.040 --> 00:25:34.210
is extremely good karma.

00:25:34.210 --> 00:25:35.983
Extremely good karma. Great karma.

00:25:35.983 --> 00:25:37.770
THEG PA CHEN PO'I CHOS DANG PHRAD

00:25:37.770 --> 00:25:40.560
BLANG DOR YANG CUNG ZAD SHES

00:25:40.560 --> 00:25:43.493
We understand what we should
do, and what we shouldn't do,

00:25:43.493 --> 00:25:46.803
CUNG ZAD - a tiny bit.

00:25:48.489 --> 00:25:50.314
A tiny bit - CUNG ZAD.

00:25:50.314 --> 00:25:52.510
We understand a tiny bit
about what we should do

00:25:52.510 --> 00:25:54.018
or shouldn't do.

00:25:54.018 --> 00:25:56.645
DE DAG LAS RANG CHES CHER BZANG BAS

00:25:56.645 --> 00:25:58.233
In that sense

00:26:00.637 --> 00:26:05.610
we are more blessed than our mom,

00:26:05.610 --> 00:26:09.276
the blind crazy mom.

00:26:09.276 --> 00:26:11.670
We have some eyes.

00:26:11.670 --> 00:26:14.240
We have some sanity.

00:26:14.240 --> 00:26:17.920
We are following Lam Rim.
That's a sign of sanity.

00:26:17.920 --> 00:26:22.330
So I'm not the best person in the world,

00:26:22.330 --> 00:26:25.890
but compared to someone
who never heard Lam Rim,

00:26:25.890 --> 00:26:28.250
or never heard that you
should take care other people,

00:26:28.250 --> 00:26:30.933
I'm like perfect.

00:26:30.933 --> 00:26:34.040
Here is a funny word - CHES CHER BZANG.

00:26:34.040 --> 00:26:38.340
I'm like super. I'm really perfect,

00:26:38.340 --> 00:26:40.030
compared to these other people

00:26:40.030 --> 00:26:42.580
who are blind and crazy.

00:26:42.580 --> 00:26:46.070
At least I have eyes. I
don't use them very well.

00:26:46.070 --> 00:26:48.880
And at least I'm not crazy.

00:26:48.880 --> 00:26:52.383
Although it's crazy to act
crazy when you don't have to.

00:26:53.952 --> 00:26:56.800
DE DAG DE LAS SKYOB THABS KYI KHUR BYED

00:26:56.800 --> 00:27:01.200
The KHUR [burden] to take care
of my mom has fallen to me

00:27:01.200 --> 00:27:03.870
because I am the only one
who has any eyes around here.

00:27:03.870 --> 00:27:07.006
I'm the only one who
has Lam Rim around here.

00:27:07.006 --> 00:27:08.203
BYED MKHAN RANG LA BABS TSUL

00:27:08.203 --> 00:27:12.570
BABS TSUL means it has come down to me.

00:27:12.570 --> 00:27:15.930
There's nobody else who can
take this responsibility.

00:27:15.930 --> 00:27:19.650
It's all fallen - BABS - to me - BSAM PA.

00:27:19.650 --> 00:27:22.150
So think about that.

00:27:22.150 --> 00:27:24.995
I like this picture

00:27:25.955 --> 00:27:28.120
of giving CPR to somebody,

00:27:28.120 --> 00:27:30.331
trying to save somebody's live who's...

00:27:32.517 --> 00:27:34.590
I don't know if you've had
this happen in your life.

00:27:34.590 --> 00:27:39.440
If you live as long as
me and Jigme, it happens,

00:27:39.440 --> 00:27:40.880
every 20 years or something

00:27:40.880 --> 00:27:44.830
that you get to save somebody's life.

00:27:44.830 --> 00:27:46.600
I remember somebody was on fire

00:27:46.600 --> 00:27:51.533
and I was able to knock
them down and save them.

00:27:51.533 --> 00:27:53.930
So in your...or in a car accident,

00:27:53.930 --> 00:27:55.690
I pulled somebody out of a car.

00:27:55.690 --> 00:27:57.290
It doesn't happen very often.

00:27:59.210 --> 00:28:01.877
But it seems like a high honor

00:28:01.877 --> 00:28:04.872
to have the chance to save a life.

00:28:04.872 --> 00:28:07.010
Someone is going to die

00:28:07.010 --> 00:28:10.650
if you don't do something
in the next two minutes.

00:28:10.650 --> 00:28:14.850
And for some reason you don't freak out

00:28:14.850 --> 00:28:16.530
and you think clearly for two minutes,

00:28:16.530 --> 00:28:17.540
And you pull them out of the car

00:28:17.540 --> 00:28:19.610
and the car blows up. And you are like,

00:28:19.610 --> 00:28:21.330
"Damn, I did it."

00:28:21.330 --> 00:28:23.450
And it happens a few times in your life.

00:28:23.450 --> 00:28:25.956
It's one of the sweetest things in life

00:28:25.956 --> 00:28:28.767
to be able to say I save somebody's life

00:28:28.767 --> 00:28:30.400
is a great feeling.

00:28:30.400 --> 00:28:32.700
It's one of the greatest feelings in life.

00:28:32.700 --> 00:28:37.550
So anyway, you have a chance
right now to save your mom.

00:28:37.550 --> 00:28:42.200
Your mom's had a car accident.
The car is about to blow up.

00:28:43.547 --> 00:28:45.360
And all of us have this chance

00:28:45.360 --> 00:28:48.636
to pull our mom out of the car.

00:28:48.636 --> 00:28:49.830
YANG SLOB SPRING LAS

00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:53.026
This is called A letter to a Student.

00:28:53.026 --> 00:28:56.126
It was written by Master Chandragomi

00:28:56.126 --> 00:29:00.986
about 1,300 or 1,400 years ago.

00:29:00.986 --> 00:29:04.011
,NYE DU 'KHOR BA'I RGYA
MTSO'I KHONGS SU CHUD GYUR PA,

00:29:04.011 --> 00:29:07.036
,KLONG GI NANG DU LHUNG
BA LTA BUR SNANG BZHIN DU,

00:29:07.036 --> 00:29:10.297
,SKYE SHI 'PHOS PAS NGO
MA SHES PA DE BOR NAS,

00:29:10.297 --> 00:29:14.414
,GAL TE GCIG THAR BYED
NA DE LAS KHREL BOR MED.

00:29:14.414 --> 00:29:18.806
NYE DU means your loved
one, the people you love,

00:29:18.806 --> 00:29:21.508
'KHOR BA'I RGYA MTSO
KHONGS SU CHUD GYUR PA

00:29:21.508 --> 00:29:26.207
they have fallen into
the ocean of sansara,

00:29:26.207 --> 00:29:27.584
suffering life.

00:29:27.584 --> 00:29:29.580
KLONG GI NANG DU LHUNG

00:29:29.580 --> 00:29:31.349
And there's a, what do you call that?

00:29:31.349 --> 00:29:33.547
a whirlpool.

00:29:33.547 --> 00:29:37.416
What do you call that? Because
there's another one for that.

00:29:38.540 --> 00:29:40.570
Thers' a technical word for whirlpool

00:29:40.570 --> 00:29:42.273
in the middle of the ocean.

00:29:45.760 --> 00:29:47.760
It's like a vortex. Huh?

00:29:49.400 --> 00:29:52.840
I don't know. You can check.

00:29:52.840 --> 00:29:57.530
But anyway, your mom has
fallen into this whirlpool

00:29:57.530 --> 00:29:59.887
in the middle of the ocean.

00:29:59.887 --> 00:30:02.710
SNANG BZHIN DU, SKYE SHI 'PHOS PAS

00:30:02.710 --> 00:30:06.790
She's moving from birth
to death, birth to death,

00:30:06.790 --> 00:30:07.623
birth to death.

00:30:08.674 --> 00:30:10.410
NGO MA SHES PA

00:30:10.410 --> 00:30:13.390
Because she's been shifting
from birth to death,

00:30:13.390 --> 00:30:14.223
and birth and death,

00:30:14.223 --> 00:30:17.270
and because you've been
switching from birth to death

00:30:17.270 --> 00:30:21.053
to birth to death, you
don't recognize her.

00:30:21.053 --> 00:30:24.740
NGO MA SHES means you don't recognize

00:30:24.740 --> 00:30:26.270
that she was your mom,

00:30:26.270 --> 00:30:30.683
because there's been too
many deaths in between.

00:30:31.707 --> 00:30:32.540
BOR NAS

00:30:32.540 --> 00:30:34.953
And so you ignore her.

00:30:37.601 --> 00:30:39.500
GAL TE GCIG THAR BYED NA

00:30:39.500 --> 00:30:42.420
And you kind of say, I'm
going to focus on myself.

00:30:42.420 --> 00:30:45.183
I think I'll just focus on myself.

00:30:46.630 --> 00:30:48.920
I know these other people are suffering

00:30:48.920 --> 00:30:52.950
but they are not... There's no big reason

00:30:52.950 --> 00:30:55.840
why I should take care of them also.

00:30:55.840 --> 00:30:58.634
You don't recognize that
they have been your mom.

00:30:58.634 --> 00:31:01.393
DE LAS KHREL BOR MED

00:31:03.946 --> 00:31:08.890
KHREL MED means you don't
care what others think.

00:31:08.890 --> 00:31:11.840
Remember? When you do a bad deed

00:31:11.840 --> 00:31:13.890
and you don't care
about what others think,

00:31:13.890 --> 00:31:14.910
that's called KHREL MED

00:31:14.910 --> 00:31:19.800
So here it means how could
you do anything more shameless

00:31:19.800 --> 00:31:23.620
than to ignore your mom if
she's in the middle of drowning,

00:31:23.620 --> 00:31:25.510
and you're just swimming off by yourself.

00:31:25.510 --> 00:31:27.349
Did you find that thing?

00:31:27.349 --> 00:31:30.349
[TL] I think that word
is maelstrom. [GMR] Yes.

00:31:32.060 --> 00:31:33.719
I think maelstrom.

00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:38.044
Yes. That sounds good.

00:31:38.044 --> 00:31:40.377
CES PA LTAR MA SEMS CAN
'KHOR BA'I RGYA MTSO'I

00:31:40.377 --> 00:31:43.085
KLONG DU CHUD PA RNAMS
DA RES RANG LA 'DON PA'I

00:31:43.085 --> 00:31:45.520
THABS YOD BZHIN DU

00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:50.070
Your mom fell into the
ocean. She's being suck down

00:31:50.070 --> 00:31:54.320
by a maelstrom, whirlpool.

00:31:54.320 --> 00:31:58.580
And you have... What
do you call those thing

00:31:58.580 --> 00:32:02.020
you throw to the drowning
people? The ring.

00:32:02.020 --> 00:32:02.958
- [Woman] Life saver.

00:32:02.958 --> 00:32:05.166
- [GMR] Yes, you have the life ring?

00:32:05.166 --> 00:32:06.291
- [Woman] Life saver.

00:32:06.291 --> 00:32:07.940
- [GMR] Life saver?

00:32:07.940 --> 00:32:10.450
Yes, and then you're just standing there

00:32:10.450 --> 00:32:12.650
with the life saver and
you don't throw it to her?

00:32:12.650 --> 00:32:13.930
What's wrong with you?

00:32:13.930 --> 00:32:15.730
What kind of person are you?

00:32:15.730 --> 00:32:19.490
Like you have a way called Lam Rim

00:32:19.490 --> 00:32:21.210
and you could just throw to her,

00:32:21.210 --> 00:32:24.363
and you're like, "Huh? What?
Oh, look she's drowning..."

00:32:26.103 --> 00:32:28.510
THABS YOD BZHIN DU MA BTON NA

00:32:28.510 --> 00:32:30.610
If you don't pull her out,

00:32:30.610 --> 00:32:31.840
MA RABS

00:32:31.840 --> 00:32:34.490
You should learn this word MA RABS.

00:32:34.490 --> 00:32:37.360
MA RABS has nothing to do with mother.

00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:40.670
And it has nothing to do with not really.

00:32:40.670 --> 00:32:44.320
MA RABS means

00:32:44.320 --> 00:32:45.820
worst of the worst.

00:32:45.820 --> 00:32:47.490
It's a useful word.

00:32:48.657 --> 00:32:50.012
MA RABS

00:32:50.012 --> 00:32:54.170
MA RABS THA CHAD means you
are the worst of the worst

00:32:54.170 --> 00:32:55.630
of all the people in the world.

00:32:55.630 --> 00:32:58.880
You just really suck.

00:32:58.880 --> 00:33:01.120
You stand there at the life preserver

00:33:01.120 --> 00:33:04.262
and you watch your mom go
under. What's wrong with you?

00:33:04.262 --> 00:33:05.930
That's MA RABS THA CHAD.

00:33:05.930 --> 00:33:08.273
You are like the worst of the worst.

00:33:09.367 --> 00:33:11.890
DE DAG 'DON PA'I KHUR DA RES

00:33:11.890 --> 00:33:15.950
The KHUR, the responsibility or the burden

00:33:15.950 --> 00:33:20.233
of pulling her out, which is 'DON.

00:33:22.495 --> 00:33:25.133
DA RES RANG NYID LA BABS

00:33:25.133 --> 00:33:28.160
BABS means the responsibility has fallen

00:33:28.160 --> 00:33:29.730
on your shoulders.

00:33:29.730 --> 00:33:33.770
So do it. 'DUG SNYAM DU DRIN GZO BSGOM

00:33:33.770 --> 00:33:38.040
And that what it means to meditate

00:33:38.040 --> 00:33:40.010
on repaying your mother's kindness.

00:33:40.010 --> 00:33:43.510
So it's interesting. She gave you food.

00:33:43.510 --> 00:33:46.800
She gave you language.
She gave you walking.

00:33:46.800 --> 00:33:50.750
She gave you manners. She
gave you wearing clothes.

00:33:50.750 --> 00:33:53.620
And when you say, you should pay her back

00:33:53.620 --> 00:33:55.650
it feels like... Oh, you should feed her.

00:33:55.650 --> 00:33:58.680
Or you should make sure she has clothes.

00:33:58.680 --> 00:34:00.970
Or you should teach her Spanish

00:34:00.970 --> 00:34:03.103
if she's speaking English or something.

00:34:03.103 --> 00:34:04.550
And he says, no no no,

00:34:04.550 --> 00:34:07.853
just save her life, okay, it's enough.

00:34:09.040 --> 00:34:11.280
We're not talking about paying her back

00:34:11.280 --> 00:34:13.150
with what she gave you,

00:34:13.150 --> 00:34:16.570
we're talking about saving her life.

00:34:16.570 --> 00:34:19.900
That's a difference. You can pay her back

00:34:19.900 --> 00:34:21.830
not by buying her new dress

00:34:21.830 --> 00:34:24.763
or by buying her a nice French dinner.

00:34:24.763 --> 00:34:28.310
How about you just save her
life? That would be nice.

00:34:29.450 --> 00:34:32.269
DRIN GZO BA DE YANG DBU MA SNYING PO LAS

00:34:32.269 --> 00:34:34.477
Then he quotes a book called the

00:34:34.477 --> 00:34:36.220
Essence of the Middle Way,

00:34:36.220 --> 00:34:39.840
which is a famous book
by Master Bhavaviveka,

00:34:39.840 --> 00:34:41.490
Lower Middle Way.

00:34:42.916 --> 00:34:46.278
,GZHAN YANG SNGON CHAD NYON MONGS PA'I,

00:34:46.278 --> 00:34:47.870
,GDON GYIS BRLAMS PA BDAG GIS NI,

00:34:47.870 --> 00:34:51.528
SNGON CHAD means in the past.

00:34:51.528 --> 00:34:54.003
NYON MONGS PA'I GDON GYIS BRLAMS PA

00:34:54.003 --> 00:34:56.990
What do you call that when a
spirit takes over a person?

00:34:56.990 --> 00:34:57.860
- [Tim] Possession.

00:34:57.860 --> 00:35:02.550
- [GMR] Possession. Yes. I
was possessed by the demon.

00:35:02.550 --> 00:35:05.770
I have been possessed by the demon

00:35:05.770 --> 00:35:08.960
of my own negative emotions.

00:35:08.960 --> 00:35:10.493
And because of that,

00:35:12.670 --> 00:35:15.262
instead of trying to help my mom,

00:35:15.262 --> 00:35:17.213
RMAS LA 'GYUR BYED

00:35:17.213 --> 00:35:19.540
'GYUR BYED is an interesting word.

00:35:19.540 --> 00:35:21.570
It means the changer, right Tim?

00:35:21.570 --> 00:35:25.530
'GYUR BYED - the changer.
And it's a word for salt

00:35:25.530 --> 00:35:28.343
because it changes the taste of a dish.

00:35:29.680 --> 00:35:32.043
The changer.

00:35:32.043 --> 00:35:36.400
RMAS misspelled here means open wound.

00:35:36.400 --> 00:35:40.070
So I'm supposed to be the hero

00:35:40.070 --> 00:35:42.570
who goes and saves my mom.

00:35:42.570 --> 00:35:46.550
But what I've been
doing so far in my life,

00:35:46.550 --> 00:35:51.450
because I was possessed by the
demon of my own selfishness,

00:35:51.450 --> 00:35:54.170
I was rubbing salt in her wounds

00:35:54.170 --> 00:35:57.863
instead of trying to
put a band-aid on them.

00:35:57.863 --> 00:36:00.970
,SDUG BSNGAL NAD PA GANG SDUG BYAS,

00:36:00.970 --> 00:36:05.900
I was doing my best to
make her condition worse.

00:36:05.900 --> 00:36:07.520
I was pushing her off a cliff

00:36:07.520 --> 00:36:09.440
after she went blind and crazy.

00:36:09.440 --> 00:36:11.720
And I was like leading her to the

00:36:11.720 --> 00:36:14.844
to the edge of the cliff.

00:36:14.844 --> 00:36:16.560
,SKYE BA GZHAN DU GANG DAG GIS,

00:36:16.560 --> 00:36:18.535
,BYAMS DANG BSNYEN BKUR PHAN PA BYAS,

00:36:19.990 --> 00:36:24.300
Look, in other lives,
the people around you

00:36:24.300 --> 00:36:26.984
have cared for you,

00:36:26.984 --> 00:36:29.620
as literally as your mother.

00:36:29.620 --> 00:36:30.810
They have BYAMS PA.

00:36:30.810 --> 00:36:32.030
They have shown you BYAMS PA.

00:36:32.030 --> 00:36:33.940
What's that, you guys?

00:36:33.940 --> 00:36:36.303
Love. And BSNYEN BKUR

00:36:36.303 --> 00:36:39.980
BSNYEN BKUR means they have respected you

00:36:39.980 --> 00:36:41.233
and cared for you.

00:36:41.233 --> 00:36:46.233
PHAN PA - They have given you
help your whole life long.

00:36:46.240 --> 00:36:47.606
And in return,

00:36:48.798 --> 00:36:50.906
LAN DU PHAN GDAGS PA

00:36:50.906 --> 00:36:54.600
wouldn't you want to repay them in kind?

00:36:54.600 --> 00:36:57.980
Wouldn't you want to give them
back the same kind of help?

00:36:57.980 --> 00:36:59.593
What's the best one you can do?

00:36:59.593 --> 00:37:03.130
MYA NGAN BZLA as a verb.

00:37:03.130 --> 00:37:06.221
We had an in the Diamond Cutter Sutra.

00:37:08.471 --> 00:37:10.780
MYA NGAN BZLA

00:37:10.780 --> 00:37:12.805
Nirvanacize.

00:37:14.050 --> 00:37:15.990
So here is a very strange verb.

00:37:15.990 --> 00:37:19.028
It's almost an invented verb.

00:37:19.028 --> 00:37:22.450
,MYA NGAN BLZA LAS GZHAN CI YOD,

00:37:22.450 --> 00:37:24.773
There's no option.

00:37:26.120 --> 00:37:28.290
Don't give them clothes back.

00:37:28.290 --> 00:37:31.600
Don't give them food back. Give them back

00:37:31.600 --> 00:37:34.330
nirvana and buddhahood. That's repayment.

00:37:34.330 --> 00:37:36.200
That's DRIN GZO.

00:37:36.200 --> 00:37:39.100
That's paying your mom back.

00:37:39.100 --> 00:37:40.970
It's kind of common, right?

00:37:40.970 --> 00:37:42.230
If someone gives you a gift

00:37:42.230 --> 00:37:44.770
you're try to give them back
something better, right?

00:37:44.770 --> 00:37:47.760
So, okay, you gave me
food. You gave me language.

00:37:47.760 --> 00:37:50.450
You gave me walking. You
gave me dressing clothes.

00:37:50.450 --> 00:37:52.183
You gave me human behavior.

00:37:53.260 --> 00:37:55.220
I think I'll give you nirvana back

00:37:55.220 --> 00:37:57.278
or buddhahood if you want.

00:37:57.278 --> 00:37:59.430
That's a good deal.

00:37:59.430 --> 00:38:00.263
All right.

00:38:02.205 --> 00:38:03.470
That's the picture we have here

00:38:03.470 --> 00:38:05.690
that we started out the class with.

00:38:05.690 --> 00:38:08.765
Is this, you know,

00:38:08.765 --> 00:38:11.190
the idea of the young girl,

00:38:11.190 --> 00:38:13.520
she's paying her mom back.

00:38:13.520 --> 00:38:15.150
She's giving her something beautiful.

00:38:15.150 --> 00:38:18.590
The most beautiful things
you can give to your mom

00:38:18.590 --> 00:38:21.473
to pay her back is nirvana and buddhahood.

00:38:21.473 --> 00:38:24.640
CES PA LTAR ZAS DANG GOS
SOGS STER BA TZAM GYIS NI

00:38:24.640 --> 00:38:27.622
Yeah you can give her food,
you can give her clothes.

00:38:27.622 --> 00:38:29.740
GNAS SKABS KYI BKRES SKOM LAS GROL TZAM

00:38:29.740 --> 00:38:31.510
She will reach a liberation

00:38:32.530 --> 00:38:35.937
but only from hunger and thirst,

00:38:37.370 --> 00:38:39.441
physical hunger, physical thirst.

00:38:39.441 --> 00:38:41.987
LAS PHUGS SU PHAN PA ZHIG MI 'BYUNG

00:38:41.987 --> 00:38:44.904
PHUGS SU means in the longterm.

00:38:46.080 --> 00:38:48.520
She doesn't get... You can...

00:38:48.520 --> 00:38:52.634
It's very common to buy your mom a TV

00:38:52.634 --> 00:38:54.676
or an apartment even,

00:38:54.676 --> 00:38:56.203
or something like that.

00:38:57.470 --> 00:39:00.087
And he says, okay, that's
help, that's PHAN PA,

00:39:00.087 --> 00:39:01.210
but not PHUGS SU.

00:39:01.210 --> 00:39:04.893
That's not ultimately going
to help her that much.

00:39:04.893 --> 00:39:06.116
BDE BA THAMS CAD DANG LDAN PA DANG

00:39:06.116 --> 00:39:08.970
SDUG BSNGAL THAMS CAD
DANG BRAL BA ZHIG BYUNG NA

00:39:08.970 --> 00:39:13.260
If she could get every form of happiness,

00:39:13.260 --> 00:39:16.712
and if she could escape
every form of pain,

00:39:16.712 --> 00:39:19.440
SEMS CAN DE DAG LA'ANG
PHAN PA BRTAN CING CHE LA

00:39:19.440 --> 00:39:23.900
That's real payback.
That's a good pay back.

00:39:23.900 --> 00:39:27.020
Give her every form of happiness

00:39:27.020 --> 00:39:28.780
and remove every form of pain.

00:39:28.780 --> 00:39:30.043
That's a good pay back.

00:39:30.043 --> 00:39:32.520
DE YANG SANGS RGYAS KYI
GO 'PHANG LA BKOD NA

00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:36.860
Now if you could push her to buddhahood,

00:39:36.860 --> 00:39:40.280
if you could get her to go to buddhahood,

00:39:40.280 --> 00:39:41.730
Yes, then BDE BA THAMS CAD,

00:39:41.730 --> 00:39:44.022
she gets everything she ever wanted.

00:39:44.022 --> 00:39:45.400
SDUG BSNGAL THAMS CAD DANG BRAL

00:39:45.400 --> 00:39:48.095
She gets free of every
pain she ever wanted.

00:39:48.095 --> 00:39:50.086
YIN PAS SEMS CAN THAMS CAD
SANGS RGYAS KYI GO 'PHANG LA

00:39:50.086 --> 00:39:52.100
'GCOD PAR BYA'O SNYAM PA DGOS

00:39:52.100 --> 00:39:56.270
Therefore, because
everyone has been your mom,

00:39:56.270 --> 00:40:00.450
your motivation should
be to pay them back.

00:40:00.450 --> 00:40:02.810
I'll push all of them into buddhahood.

00:40:02.810 --> 00:40:07.810
I'll be the pusher. I will
get them into buddhahood.

00:40:08.099 --> 00:40:11.560
DPER NA, RANG GI AA MA
SMYO NAS GRI KHYER TE

00:40:11.560 --> 00:40:14.920
I love this image.

00:40:14.920 --> 00:40:17.670
I went through this Lam Rim
three times with my teacher

00:40:17.670 --> 00:40:20.469
over 30 years.

00:40:20.469 --> 00:40:23.901
And I loved this image.

00:40:23.901 --> 00:40:24.734
RANG GI AA MA

00:40:24.734 --> 00:40:27.250
We use it a lot in DCI.

00:40:27.250 --> 00:40:30.770
Suppose, I like to tell the story

00:40:30.770 --> 00:40:34.453
because it happened kind of to me.

00:40:34.453 --> 00:40:37.011
A friend of mine's mom,

00:40:37.011 --> 00:40:39.502
who was living alone,

00:40:39.502 --> 00:40:41.493
I was helping to take care of her

00:40:41.493 --> 00:40:43.330
from time to time.

00:40:43.330 --> 00:40:46.973
She had to take her meds every morning.

00:40:46.973 --> 00:40:50.210
Later we had the hire someone

00:40:50.210 --> 00:40:51.600
to give her her meds every morning

00:40:51.600 --> 00:40:53.130
because she would take the wrong ones

00:40:53.130 --> 00:40:54.290
or she would take the whole bottle.

00:40:54.290 --> 00:40:56.930
She took a whole bottle of something.

00:40:56.930 --> 00:41:00.810
And she went... What you
call it? Temporary insanity.

00:41:01.910 --> 00:41:05.350
And she was cooking, and
she was cutting vegetables

00:41:05.350 --> 00:41:06.783
with a big knife.

00:41:07.810 --> 00:41:10.230
You can see the picture here.

00:41:10.230 --> 00:41:12.160
It took me so long to find this picture.

00:41:12.160 --> 00:41:13.203
I don't know why.

00:41:15.140 --> 00:41:19.630
Yes, she was cutting vegetables
with this big meat cleaver.

00:41:19.630 --> 00:41:22.330
And we told her...We went to the store.

00:41:22.330 --> 00:41:24.040
We said we're coming back.

00:41:24.040 --> 00:41:26.200
And we're coming back,

00:41:26.200 --> 00:41:29.030
and we were trying to get the lock open

00:41:29.030 --> 00:41:31.110
because she has sliding glass door

00:41:31.110 --> 00:41:32.730
and it didn't work very well.

00:41:32.730 --> 00:41:36.480
And she forgot that we were coming

00:41:36.480 --> 00:41:38.660
And she thought it was a robber

00:41:38.660 --> 00:41:40.470
or someone come to hurt her.

00:41:40.470 --> 00:41:42.030
And she picked up the knife

00:41:42.030 --> 00:41:44.570
And she heads towards the door.

00:41:44.570 --> 00:41:48.207
And we were like, "Oh,
no, no, no! It's us!"

00:41:48.207 --> 00:41:51.310
But when a ninety years
old woman is scared,

00:41:51.310 --> 00:41:53.260
and she's got this cleaver in her hand,

00:41:53.260 --> 00:41:55.210
and sometimes...

00:41:58.806 --> 00:42:01.970
and this is the answer to a
question that you will get

00:42:01.970 --> 00:42:05.650
as a Buddhist many, many
times from other people.

00:42:05.650 --> 00:42:07.990
Okay, you're a Buddhist. Yes.

00:42:07.990 --> 00:42:10.470
So what do you do if somebody attacks you?

00:42:10.470 --> 00:42:13.510
If another country attacks you?

00:42:14.540 --> 00:42:16.720
Or if a person attacks you with a knife?

00:42:16.720 --> 00:42:18.600
Then what are you going to do?

00:42:18.600 --> 00:42:20.820
What's the right thing to do?

00:42:20.820 --> 00:42:24.530
The classic answer that you should learn

00:42:24.530 --> 00:42:26.910
if you are going to teach Lam Rim

00:42:26.910 --> 00:42:30.630
is treat them like your own mom.

00:42:30.630 --> 00:42:35.630
If your own mom took some
extra drugs by accident

00:42:35.950 --> 00:42:39.660
and went crazy, and then
you were coming in the door,

00:42:39.660 --> 00:42:41.700
and she thought you were
someone come to hurt her

00:42:41.700 --> 00:42:44.370
and she came to you with a big knife,

00:42:44.370 --> 00:42:46.093
then would you shoot her?

00:42:47.110 --> 00:42:49.760
Would you stab her?

00:42:49.760 --> 00:42:52.540
And then no, of course I wouldn't.

00:42:52.540 --> 00:42:54.090
Well what would you do?

00:42:54.090 --> 00:42:57.900
Well, I will try to
wrestle her to the ground

00:42:57.900 --> 00:43:00.060
and try to get the knife out of her hands.

00:43:00.060 --> 00:43:02.410
Well what if she cut you?

00:43:02.410 --> 00:43:04.300
Well, that's okay. It's worth it.

00:43:04.300 --> 00:43:07.020
She gave me a few cuts.

00:43:07.020 --> 00:43:08.920
It's better than killing her.

00:43:08.920 --> 00:43:12.550
I wouldn't take a gun
and shoot my own mom.

00:43:12.550 --> 00:43:14.736
I would take a few cuts.

00:43:15.936 --> 00:43:18.540
So that's the answer to the question of

00:43:18.540 --> 00:43:20.960
what to do if someone attacks you?

00:43:20.960 --> 00:43:24.330
Try to -- What do you call that? --

00:43:24.330 --> 00:43:27.770
disabled them or disarm them.

00:43:27.770 --> 00:43:32.220
Even if it causes you
some pain or some trouble,

00:43:32.220 --> 00:43:34.590
even serious trouble, it's
better than killing them

00:43:34.590 --> 00:43:36.800
because they are your mom.
They have been your mom.

00:43:36.800 --> 00:43:39.150
You wouldn't shoot you mom

00:43:39.150 --> 00:43:41.020
if she came at you with a knife,

00:43:41.020 --> 00:43:44.293
even in America. I don't think so.

00:43:46.830 --> 00:43:48.798
So anyway, here is the Tibetan

00:43:48.798 --> 00:43:50.306
RANG GI AA MA SMYO NAS

00:43:50.306 --> 00:43:52.670
Suppose your mom went crazy,

00:43:52.670 --> 00:43:54.760
GRI KHYER TE

00:43:54.760 --> 00:43:57.506
and suppose she approached
you with a knife,

00:43:57.506 --> 00:43:59.172
BU RANG NYID GSOD PAR RTZOM

00:43:59.172 --> 00:44:04.172
RTZOM here means to undertake or to start.

00:44:04.570 --> 00:44:06.330
It can also means to write a book.

00:44:06.330 --> 00:44:07.892
So you have to be careful.

00:44:07.892 --> 00:44:11.050
RTZOM NA'ANG AA MA LA MI KHRO BAR

00:44:11.050 --> 00:44:14.240
You would not get angry at your mom.

00:44:14.240 --> 00:44:15.877
You wouldn't get furious and say,

00:44:15.877 --> 00:44:18.140
"Mom, I'm going to kill you."

00:44:18.140 --> 00:44:21.150
MI PHRO BAR SMYO NAD DE SEL THABS

00:44:21.150 --> 00:44:23.450
You would try to knock her down

00:44:23.450 --> 00:44:26.217
and you would try to keep her safe

00:44:26.217 --> 00:44:31.213
until the craziness passed from her mind.

00:44:31.213 --> 00:44:32.046
BRTZON DGOS PA

00:44:32.046 --> 00:44:34.500
You have to work hard to do it that way.

00:44:34.500 --> 00:44:38.070
BZHIN DU DGRA LA'ANG DRIN GZO BYA DGOS

00:44:38.070 --> 00:44:42.490
Then Pabongka Rinpoche ends this section

00:44:42.490 --> 00:44:44.017
by saying,

00:44:44.017 --> 00:44:48.437
I'm talking about people
who've been your mother

00:44:48.437 --> 00:44:50.887
who are your enemy in this life.

00:44:50.887 --> 00:44:54.853
I'm talking about people
who hurt you in this life:

00:44:54.853 --> 00:44:57.480
people in your business,

00:44:57.480 --> 00:45:01.092
other business executives
who trying to screw you,

00:45:01.092 --> 00:45:05.214
or other country's people
who are attack your country

00:45:05.214 --> 00:45:08.030
and try to kill you or hurt you,

00:45:08.030 --> 00:45:10.360
people in your family who are jealous

00:45:10.360 --> 00:45:13.590
or do things to hurt you.

00:45:13.590 --> 00:45:18.460
I'm saying they have been
your mom and DRIN GZO.

00:45:18.460 --> 00:45:21.130
It's time to payback.

00:45:21.130 --> 00:45:24.057
There's a James Brown
song The Big Payback.

00:45:25.280 --> 00:45:26.600
It's time for payback.

00:45:26.600 --> 00:45:29.480
But payback in Buddhism means

00:45:29.480 --> 00:45:33.140
it's time to push them into
nirvana and buddhahood,

00:45:33.140 --> 00:45:35.110
not to pay them back by

00:45:35.110 --> 00:45:37.940
hurting them more than they hurt you.

00:45:37.940 --> 00:45:40.590
All right. Great words.
Difficult to practice.

00:45:40.590 --> 00:45:45.093
And we'll see you in the next
Lam Rim episode. Thank you.

